{"config":{"lang":["en"],"separator":"[\\s\\-_,:!=\\[\\]()\\\\\"`/]+|\\.(?!\\d)"},"items":[{"location":"","level":1,"title":"Python API","text":"<p>Native planar topology checks for Python GIS workflows.</p>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.Topology","level":2,"title":"Topology","text":"<pre><code>Topology(tolerance: float = 0.0)\n</code></pre> <p>Own planar layers, ordered rules, and reusable native topology caches.</p> <p>Parameters:</p> Name Type Description Default <code>tolerance</code> <code>float</code> <p>Nonnegative finite distance in input coordinate units.</p> <code>0.0</code> <p>Raises:</p> Type Description <code>ValueError</code> <p>Tolerance is negative or nonfinite.</p>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.Topology.tolerance","level":3,"title":"tolerance  <small><code>property</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>tolerance: float\n</code></pre> <p>Return the planar tolerance in caller-supplied coordinate units.</p>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.Topology.layers","level":3,"title":"layers  <small><code>property</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>layers: tuple[Layer, ...]\n</code></pre> <p>Return immutable layer snapshots in registration order.</p>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.Topology.layer","level":3,"title":"layer","text":"<pre><code>layer(id: LayerId) -&gt; Layer\n</code></pre> <p>Return a registered layer, rejecting IDs from other topologies.</p>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.Topology.add_layer","level":3,"title":"add_layer","text":"<pre><code>add_layer(data: Any, *, name: str | None = None, fids: Iterable[int] | None = None, crs: Any = None, kind: GeometryKind | None = None) -&gt; LayerId\n</code></pre> <p>Snapshot and register GIS data as a planar layer.</p> <p>Parameters:</p> Name Type Description Default <code>data</code> <code>Any</code> <p>Geometry iterable, GeoSeries, GeoDataFrame, GeoJSON mapping, or object implementing geo_interface.</p> required <code>name</code> <code>str | None</code> <p>Optional display label. Defaults to layer_N using registration order.</p> <code>None</code> <code>fids</code> <code>Iterable[int] | None</code> <p>Unique signed 64-bit IDs for all original input positions.</p> <code>None</code> <code>crs</code> <code>Any</code> <p>Optional CRS, which must agree with input and known layer metadata.</p> <code>None</code> <code>kind</code> <code>GeometryKind | None</code> <p>Optional POINT, LINE, or POLYGON declaration for ambiguous data.</p> <code>None</code> <p>Returns:</p> Type Description <code>LayerId</code> <p>An identity scoped to this topology.</p> <p>Raises:</p> Type Description <code>TypeError</code> <p>Input data, the name, or the declaration has an unsupported type.</p> <code>ValueError</code> <p>Coordinates, FIDs, geometry, or CRS metadata are invalid.</p> <code>RuntimeError</code> <p>An input callback tries to register on this topology.</p>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.Topology.add_rule","level":3,"title":"add_rule","text":"<pre><code>add_rule(rule: Rule, data: Any, *, other: Any = None) -&gt; RuleSpec\n</code></pre> <p>Snapshot raw GIS inputs or reuse IDs, then atomically register a rule.</p> <p>Each raw input creates a fresh snapshot. Pass a LayerId to reuse a layer.</p> <p>Parameters:</p> Name Type Description Default <code>rule</code> <code>Rule</code> <p>Rule member. Deserialize strings explicitly with Rule(value).</p> required <code>data</code> <code>Any</code> <p>Primary GIS input or a LayerId from this topology.</p> required <code>other</code> <code>Any</code> <p>Optional secondary GIS input or distinct registered LayerId.</p> <code>None</code> <p>Returns:</p> Type Description <code>RuleSpec</code> <p>The immutable specification, including reusable IDs and native semantics.</p> <p>Raises:</p> Type Description <code>TypeError</code> <p>The rule or input has an unsupported type.</p> <code>ValueError</code> <p>IDs, families, arity, coordinates, FIDs, or CRS are invalid. Failed calls leave registrations and visible warnings unchanged.</p> <code>RuntimeError</code> <p>An input callback tries to register on this topology.</p>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.Topology.warnings","level":3,"title":"warnings","text":"<pre><code>warnings() -&gt; tuple[str, ...]\n</code></pre> <p>Return input, degenerate-part, and combined CRS warnings.</p>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.Topology.iter_validate","level":3,"title":"iter_validate","text":"<pre><code>iter_validate(batch_size: int = 1024) -&gt; ValidationStream\n</code></pre> <p>Stream a snapshot in bounded binary batches, closing it on early exit.</p> <p>Parameters:</p> Name Type Description Default <code>batch_size</code> <code>int</code> <p>Positive maximum number of buffered violations.</p> <code>1024</code> <p>Returns:</p> Type Description <code>ValidationStream</code> <p>A closeable iterator, with final summary after exhaustion.</p>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.Topology.validate","level":3,"title":"validate","text":"<pre><code>validate() -&gt; Report\n</code></pre> <p>Run native validation and return an eager immutable report.</p>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.ErrorType","level":2,"title":"ErrorType","text":"<p>               Bases: <code>Enum</code></p> <p>Deterministically ordered topology violation categories.</p>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.ErrorType.OVERLAP","level":3,"title":"OVERLAP  <small><code>class-attribute</code></small> <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>OVERLAP = 'overlap'\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.ErrorType.OUTSIDE","level":3,"title":"OUTSIDE  <small><code>class-attribute</code></small> <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>OUTSIDE = 'outside'\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.ErrorType.DANGLE","level":3,"title":"DANGLE  <small><code>class-attribute</code></small> <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>DANGLE = 'dangle'\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.ErrorType.PSEUDO_NODE","level":3,"title":"PSEUDO_NODE  <small><code>class-attribute</code></small> <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>PSEUDO_NODE = 'pseudo-node'\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.ErrorType.CROSSING","level":3,"title":"CROSSING  <small><code>class-attribute</code></small> <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>CROSSING = 'crossing'\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.ErrorType.TOUCH_INTERIOR","level":3,"title":"TOUCH_INTERIOR  <small><code>class-attribute</code></small> <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>TOUCH_INTERIOR = 'touch-interior'\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.ErrorType.SELF_OVERLAP","level":3,"title":"SELF_OVERLAP  <small><code>class-attribute</code></small> <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>SELF_OVERLAP = 'self-overlap'\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.ErrorType.SELF_CROSSING","level":3,"title":"SELF_CROSSING  <small><code>class-attribute</code></small> <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>SELF_CROSSING = 'self-crossing'\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.ErrorType.GAP","level":3,"title":"GAP  <small><code>class-attribute</code></small> <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>GAP = 'gap'\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.ErrorType.OUTER_BOUNDARY","level":3,"title":"OUTER_BOUNDARY  <small><code>class-attribute</code></small> <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>OUTER_BOUNDARY = 'outer-boundary'\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.ErrorType.MULTIPART","level":3,"title":"MULTIPART  <small><code>class-attribute</code></small> <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>MULTIPART = 'multipart'\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.ErrorType.NOT_COVERED","level":3,"title":"NOT_COVERED  <small><code>class-attribute</code></small> <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>NOT_COVERED = 'not-covered'\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.ErrorType.MISSING_POINT","level":3,"title":"MISSING_POINT  <small><code>class-attribute</code></small> <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>MISSING_POINT = 'missing-point'\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.ErrorType.POINT_COUNT","level":3,"title":"POINT_COUNT  <small><code>class-attribute</code></small> <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>POINT_COUNT = 'point-count'\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.ErrorType.CONTAINED","level":3,"title":"CONTAINED  <small><code>class-attribute</code></small> <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>CONTAINED = 'contained'\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.ErrorType.INTERSECTION","level":3,"title":"INTERSECTION  <small><code>class-attribute</code></small> <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>INTERSECTION = 'intersection'\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.GeometryKind","level":2,"title":"GeometryKind","text":"<p>               Bases: <code>Enum</code></p> <p>Geometry families accepted by a rule.</p>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.GeometryKind.POINT","level":3,"title":"POINT  <small><code>class-attribute</code></small> <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>POINT = 'point'\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.GeometryKind.LINE","level":3,"title":"LINE  <small><code>class-attribute</code></small> <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>LINE = 'line'\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.GeometryKind.POLYGON","level":3,"title":"POLYGON  <small><code>class-attribute</code></small> <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>POLYGON = 'polygon'\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.GeometryKind.COLLECTION","level":3,"title":"COLLECTION  <small><code>class-attribute</code></small> <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>COLLECTION = 'collection'\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.GeometryKind.ANY","level":3,"title":"ANY  <small><code>class-attribute</code></small> <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>ANY = 'any'\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.Rule","level":2,"title":"Rule","text":"<p>               Bases: <code>Enum</code></p> <p>Geometry-independent rules in first-occurrence Rust registry order.</p>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.Rule.MUST_NOT_OVERLAP","level":3,"title":"MUST_NOT_OVERLAP  <small><code>class-attribute</code></small> <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>MUST_NOT_OVERLAP = 'must-not-overlap'\n</code></pre>","path":["API r