'\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.Rule.MUST_BE_PROPERLY_INSIDE","level":3,"title":"MUST_BE_PROPERLY_INSIDE  <small><code>class-attribute</code></small> <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>MUST_BE_PROPERLY_INSIDE = 'must-be-properly-inside'\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.Rule.MUST_NOT_OVERLAP_BOUNDARIES","level":3,"title":"MUST_NOT_OVERLAP_BOUNDARIES  <small><code>class-attribute</code></small> <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>MUST_NOT_OVERLAP_BOUNDARIES = 'must-not-overlap-boundaries'\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.Rule.ENDPOINTS_MUST_BE_COVERED_BY_BOUNDARIES","level":3,"title":"ENDPOINTS_MUST_BE_COVERED_BY_BOUNDARIES  <small><code>class-attribute</code></small> <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>ENDPOINTS_MUST_BE_COVERED_BY_BOUNDARIES = 'endpoints-must-be-covered-by-boundaries'\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.Rule.MUST_NOT_CONTAIN","level":3,"title":"MUST_NOT_CONTAIN  <small><code>class-attribute</code></small> <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>MUST_NOT_CONTAIN = 'must-not-contain'\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.Rule.description","level":3,"title":"description  <small><code>property</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>description: str\n</code></pre> <p>Return a geometry-independent description of this constraint.</p>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.Rule.variants","level":3,"title":"variants  <small><code>property</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>variants: tuple[RuleVariant, ...]\n</code></pre> <p>Return concrete semantics in Rust registry order.</p>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.RuleVariant","level":2,"title":"RuleVariant  <small><code>dataclass</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>RuleVariant(value: str, inputs: tuple[GeometryKind, GeometryKind | None], description: str, arcgis: str | None, qgis: str | None)\n</code></pre> <p>Canonical Rust rule semantics and ordered input families.</p>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.RuleVariant.value","level":3,"title":"value  <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>value: str\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.RuleVariant.inputs","level":3,"title":"inputs  <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>inputs: tuple[GeometryKind, GeometryKind | None]\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.RuleVariant.description","level":3,"title":"description  <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>description: str\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.RuleVariant.arcgis","level":3,"title":"arcgis  <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>arcgis: str | None\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.RuleVariant.qgis","level":3,"title":"qgis  <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>qgis: str | None\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.PrecisionError","level":2,"title":"PrecisionError","text":"<p>               Bases: <code>RuntimeError</code></p> <p>Exact polygon topology could not be emitted with bounded coordinate rounding.</p>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.FeatureRef","level":2,"title":"FeatureRef  <small><code>dataclass</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>FeatureRef(layer: LayerId, fid: int, part: int | None)\n</code></pre> <p>Original feature and depth-first part position in a registered layer.</p>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.FeatureRef.layer","level":3,"title":"layer  <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>layer: LayerId\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.FeatureRef.fid","level":3,"title":"fid  <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>fid: int\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.FeatureRef.part","level":3,"title":"part  <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>part: int | None\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.FeatureRef.to_dict","level":3,"title":"to_dict","text":"<pre><code>to_dict() -&gt; dict[str, int | None]\n</code></pre> <p>Serialize a reference using its registration index.</p>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.Layer","level":2,"title":"Layer  <small><code>dataclass</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>Layer(id: LayerId, name: str, fids: tuple[int, ...], geometries: tuple[BaseGeometry, ...], crs: CRS | None, _parts: Mapping[int, tuple[int, ...]], warnings: tuple[str, ...], kind: GeometryKind | None)\n</code></pre> <p>Immutable XY snapshot of retained features and layer metadata.</p> <p>The kind is a concrete retained family, COLLECTION for mixed families, or None when unknown. Empty inputs can retain a typed hint or an explicit kind.</p>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.Layer.id","level":3,"title":"id  <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>id: LayerId\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.Layer.name","level":3,"title":"name  <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>name: str\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.Layer.fids","level":3,"title":"fids  <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>fids: tuple[int, ...]\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.Layer.geometries","level":3,"title":"geometries  <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>geometries: tuple[BaseGeometry, ...]\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.Layer.crs","level":3,"title":"crs  <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>crs: CRS | None\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.Layer.warnings","level":3,"title":"warnings  <small><code>class-attribute</code></small> <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>warnings: tuple[str, ...] = field(repr=False)\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.Layer.kind","level":3,"title":"kind  <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>kind: GeometryKind | None\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.Layer.reference","level":3,"title":"reference","text":"<pre><code>reference(fid: int, part: int | None) -&gt; FeatureRef\n</code></pre> <p>Map a native part index to original feature provenance.</p>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.LayerId","level":2,"title":"LayerId  <small><code>dataclass</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>LayerId()\n</code></pre> <p>Opaque identity scoped to the Topology that registered a layer.</p>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.LayerId.index","level":3,"title":"index  <small><code>property</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>index: int\n</code></pre> <p>Return the zero-based registration index.</p>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.LayerId.belongs_to","level":3,"title":"belongs_to","text":"<pre><code>belongs_to(owner: object) -&gt; bool\n</code></pre> <p>Check the internal topology identity token.</p>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.Report","level":2,"title":"Report  <small><code>dataclass</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>Report(tolerance: float, warnings: tuple[str, ...], rules: tuple[RuleReport, ...], crs: CRS | None)\n</code></pre> <p>A validation snapshot, independent of subsequent registrations.</p>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.Report.tolerance","level":3,"title":"tolerance  <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>tolerance: float\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.Report.warnings","level":3,"title":"warnings  <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>warnings: tuple[str, ...]\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.Report.rules","level":3,"title":"rules  <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>rules: tuple[RuleReport, ...]\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.Report.crs","level":3,"title":"crs  <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>crs: CRS | None\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.Report.violations","level":3,"title":"violations  <small><code>property</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>violations: tuple[Violation, ...]\n</code></pre> <p>Flatten violations in rule order and native deterministic order.</p>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.Report.errors","level":3,"title":"errors  <small><code>property</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>errors: tuple[Violation, ...]\n</code></pre> <p>Return flattened violations, matching Rust's report terminology.</p>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.Report.is_valid","level":3,"title":"is_valid  <small><code>property</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>is_valid: bool\n</code></pre> <p>Return whether every registered rule passed.</p>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.Report.error_count","level":3,"title":"error_count  <small><code>property</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>error_count: int\n</code></pre> <p>Return the total number of aggregated violations.</p>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.Report.to_dict","level":3,"title":"to_dict","text":"<pre><code>to_dict() -&gt; dict[str, Any]\n</code></pre> <p>Return JSON-compatible metadata, GeoJSON geometries, and enum values.</p>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.Report.to_geodataframe","level":3,"title":"to_geodataframe","text":"<pre><code>to_geodataframe() -&gt; GeoDataFrame\n</code></pre> <p>Export one row per violation, with scalar provenance columns.</p> <p>Returns:</p> Type Description <code>GeoDataFrame</code> <p>A GeoDataFrame retaining a common known CRS, including for no errors.</p> <p>Raises:</p> Type Description <code>ImportError</code> <p>The optional GeoPandas dependency is unavailable.</p>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.RuleReport","level":2,"title":"RuleReport  <small><code>dataclass</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>RuleReport(rule: Rule, layer: LayerId, other: LayerId | None, layer_name: str, other_name: str | None, counts: Mapping[ErrorType, int], violations: tuple[Violation, ...], spec: RuleSpec)\n</code></pre> <p>One registered rule's ordered violations and category counts.</p>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.RuleReport.rule","level":3,"title":"rule  <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>rule: Rule\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.RuleReport.layer","level":3,"title":"layer  <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>layer: LayerId\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.RuleReport.other","level":3,"title":"other  <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>other: LayerId | None\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.RuleReport.layer_name","level":3,"title":"layer_name  <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>layer_name: str\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.RuleReport.other_name","level":3,"title":"other_name  <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>other_name: str | None\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.RuleReport.counts","level":3,"title":"counts  <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>counts: Mapping[ErrorType, int]\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.RuleReport.violations","level":3,"title":"violations  <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>violations: tuple[Violation, ...]\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.RuleReport.spec","level":3,"title":"spec  <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>spec: RuleSpec\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.RuleReport.resolved_rule","level":3,"title":"resolved_rule  <small><code>property</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>resolved_rule: RuleVariant\n</code></pre> <p>Return the concrete rule selected during registration.</p>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.RuleReport.errors","level":3,"title":"errors  <small><code>property</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>errors: tuple[Violation, ...]\n</code></pre> <p>Return the violations, matching Rust's report terminology.</p>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.RuleReport.is_valid","level":3,"title":"is_valid  <small><code>property</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>is_valid: bool\n</code></pre> <p>Return whether this rule reported no violations.</p>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.RuleReport.error_count","level":3,"title":"error_count  <small><code>property</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>error_count: int\n</code></pre> <p>Return the number of aggregated violations.</p>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.RuleReport.to_dict","level":3,"title":"to_dict","text":"<pre><code>to_dict() -&gt; dict[str, Any]\n</code></pre> <p>Serialize this ordered rule result.</p>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.RuleSpec","level":2,"title":"RuleSpec  <small><code>dataclass</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>RuleSpec(rule: Rule, layer: LayerId, other: LayerId | None, resolved_rule: RuleVariant)\n</code></pre> <p>A registered generic constraint and its selected native semantics.</p>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.RuleSpec.rule","level":3,"title":"rule  <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>rule: Rule\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.RuleSpec.layer","level":3,"title":"layer  <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>layer: LayerId\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.RuleSpec.other","level":3,"title":"other  <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>other: LayerId | None\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.RuleSpec.resolved_rule","level":3,"title":"resolved_rule  <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>resolved_rule: RuleVariant\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.Violation","level":2,"title":"Violation  <small><code>dataclass</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>Violation(rule: Rule, error_type: ErrorType, geometry: BaseGeometry, origin: FeatureRef | None, destination: FeatureRef | None, resolved_rule: RuleVariant)\n</code></pre> <p>A topology violation with Shapely geometry and original provenance.</p>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.Violation.rule","level":3,"title":"rule  <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>rule: Rule\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.Violation.error_type","level":3,"title":"error_type  <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>error_type: ErrorType\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.Violation.geometry","level":3,"title":"geometry  <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>geometry: BaseGeometry\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.Violation.origin","level":3,"title":"origin  <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>origin: FeatureRef | None\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.Violation.destination","level":3,"title":"destination  <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>destination: FeatureRef | None\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.Violation.resolved_rule","level":3,"title":"resolved_rule  <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>resolved_rule: RuleVariant\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.Violation.to_dict","level":3,"title":"to_dict","text":"<pre><code>to_dict() -&gt; dict[str, Any]\n</code></pre> <p>Serialize enums as values and geometry as a GeoJSON mapping.</p>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.ReportSummary","level":2,"title":"ReportSummary  <small><code>dataclass</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>ReportSummary(tolerance: float, warnings: tuple[str, ...], rules: tuple[RuleSummary, ...], crs: CRS | None)\n</code></pre> <p>Final metadata available after successful stream exhaustion.</p>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.ReportSummary.tolerance","level":3,"title":"tolerance  <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>tolerance: float\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.ReportSummary.warnings","level":3,"title":"warnings  <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>warnings: tuple[str, ...]\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.ReportSummary.rules","level":3,"title":"rules  <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>rules: tuple[RuleSummary, ...]\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.ReportSummary.crs","level":3,"title":"crs  <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>crs: CRS | None\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.ReportSummary.error_count","level":3,"title":"error_count  <small><code>property</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>error_count: int\n</code></pre> <p>Return the total number of aggregated violations.</p>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.ReportSummary.is_valid","level":3,"title":"is_valid  <small><code>property</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>is_valid: bool\n</code></pre> <p>Whether every rule passed.</p>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.RuleSummary","level":2,"title":"RuleSummary  <small><code>dataclass</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>RuleSummary(spec: RuleSpec, counts: MappingProxyType[ErrorType, int], error_count: int)\n</code></pre> <p>Rule counts without retaining violation geometry.</p>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.RuleSummary.spec","level":3,"title":"spec  <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>spec: RuleSpec\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.RuleSummary.counts","level":3,"title":"counts  <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>counts: MappingProxyType[ErrorType, int]\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.RuleSummary.error_count","level":3,"title":"error_count  <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>error_count: int\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.RuleSummary.is_valid","level":3,"title":"is_valid  <small><code>property</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>is_valid: bool\n</code></pre> <p>Whether this rule passed.</p>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.ValidationStream","level":2,"title":"ValidationStream","text":"<pre><code>ValidationStream(native: NativeValidationStream, layers: tuple[Layer, ...], specs: tuple[RuleSpec, ...], warnings: tuple[str, ...], crs: CRS | None)\n</code></pre> <p>               Bases: <code>Iterator[Violation]</code></p> <p>Yield aggregated violations in deterministic rule and feature order.</p> <p>Use a context manager or close() when stopping early. The worker owns immutable snapshots; later registrations cannot change this stream. Final summary is available only after successful exhaustion, and is None after early close.</p>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.ValidationStream.summary","level":3,"title":"summary  <small><code>instance-attribute</code></small>","text":"<pre><code>summary: ReportSummary | None = None\n</code></pre>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.ValidationStream.close","level":3,"title":"close","text":"<pre><code>close() -&gt; None\n</code></pre> <p>Cancel work and release queued violations; repeated close is harmless.</p>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.explode_lines","level":2,"title":"explode_lines","text":"<pre><code>explode_lines(data: Any) -&gt; tuple[LineString, ...]\n</code></pre> <p>Return native line segments preserving input part order and direction.</p> <p>Parameters:</p> Name Type Description Default <code>data</code> <code>Any</code> <p>Any supported layer input containing only line geometries.</p> required <p>Returns:</p> Type Description <code>tuple[LineString, ...]</code> <p>Shapely LineStrings, with degenerate parts skipped.</p>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]},{"location":"#topology_checker.merge_lines","level":2,"title":"merge_lines","text":"<pre><code>merge_lines(data: Any, tolerance: float = 0.0) -&gt; tuple[LineString, ...]\n</code></pre> <p>Merge line parts through degree-two endpoint joins in native Rust.</p> <p>Parameters:</p> Name Type Description Default <code>data</code> <code>Any</code> <p>Any supported layer input containing only line geometries.</p> required <code>tolerance</code> <code>float</code> <p>Nonnegative finite distance in planar coordinate units.</p> <code>0.0</code> <p>Returns:</p> Type Description <code>tuple[LineString, ...]</code> <p>Shapely LineStrings in deterministic contributing-part order.</p>","path":["API reference"],"tags":[]}]}